# Slices 3/4 boundary: b + 1U = 3000000000U does not fit int (row size_t -> int, receiver
# lm_stg_convert_size_t_int), so the edge of the composite `return: b + 1U` refuses: `go`'s
# implicit throw `convert` (g = 3), as at a single value (unit_s4_ret_conv_range).  Uncaught, the
# root receives status 3, the entry has no value and the Message is stopped.  Mutant: the edge not
# emitted -- C narrows the composite itself and `go` completes.
fn: go () int
    size_t: b 2999999999U
    return: b + 1U
end: go
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: go(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
